i of human is apparently conserved in the great apes.</article-title><source>J Mol Evol</source><year>1995</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>250</fpage><lpage>252</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7666455</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Christian</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Fantes</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Mewborn</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ledbetter</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Large genomic duplicons map to sites of instability in the Prader-Willi/Angelman syndrome chromosome region (15q11-q13).</article-title><source>Hum Mol Genet</source><year>1999</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>1025</fpage><lpage>1037</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10332034</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ji</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Rebert</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Joslin</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Higgins</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Schultz</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicholls</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structure of the highly conserved HERC2 gene and of multiple partially duplicated paralogs in human.</article-title><source>Genome Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>319</fpage><lpage>329</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10720573</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amos-Landgraf</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ji</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Gottlieb</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Depinet</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Wandstrat</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Cassidy</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Driscoll</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rogan</surname><given-names>PK</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwartz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicholls</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chromosome breakage in the Prader-Willi and Angelman syndromes involves recombination between large, transcribed repeats at proximal and distal breakpoints.</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>1999</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>370</fpage><lpage>386</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10417280</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kent</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sugnet</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name><name><surname>Furey</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Roskin</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pringle</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Zahler</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Haussler</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The human genome browser at UCSC.</article-title><source>Genome Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>996</fpage><lpage>1006</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12045153</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>University of California Santa Cruz Genome Bioinformatics</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.genome.ucsc.edu"/></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bailey</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Yavor</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Massa</surname><given-names>HF</given-names></name><name><surname>Trask</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Eichler</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Segmental duplications: organization and impact within the current human genome project assembly.</article-title><source>Genome Res</source><year>2001</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>1005</fpage><lpage>1017</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11381028</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Riley</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Williamson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Collier</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilkie</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Makoff</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A 3-Mb map of a large segmental duplication overlapping the alpha7-nicotinic acetylcholine receptor gene (<italic>CHRNA7</italic>) at human 15q13-q14.</article-title><source>Genomics</source><year>2002</year><volume>79</volume><fpage>197</fpage><lpage>209</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11829490</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilles</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Goy</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Remache</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Manova</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Zelenetz</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cloning and characterization of a Golgin-related gene from the large-scale polymorphism linked to the PML ge