osome 15 is a susceptibility factor for panic and phobic disorders.</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>2001</year><volume>106</volume><fpage>367</fpage><lpage>379</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11509185</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pujana</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Nadal</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Guitart</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Armengol</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Gratacos</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Estivill</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human chromosome 15q11-q14 regions of rearrangements contain clusters of LCR15 duplicons.</article-title><source>Eur J Hum Genet</source><year>2002</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>26</fpage><lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11896453</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ji</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Eichler</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwartz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicholls</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structure of chromosomal duplicons and their role in mediating human genomic disorders.</article-title><source>Genome Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>597</fpage><lpage>610</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10810082</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wandstrat</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lena</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Jenkins</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwartz</surname>